  "client_brief": "Bring our painted festival wordmark into a usable anniversary kit\n\nWharfside Folk Festival is twenty years old. The shed-painted wordmark is part of that history, and we want to retain its character across the handbill, cloth and supporting anniversary materials.\n\nWhat we need back\n- Recovered festival mark: 1 named export. The source lettering is preserved.\n- Festival poster: 1 named export. The billing order follows the approved lineup. The event date is readable.\n- Festival handbill: 1 named export. The venue details are readable at print size. The ticket action is visible.\n- Festival shirt artwork: 1 named export. The ink limits follow the supplier note. The mark remains recognisable on the garment.\n\nUse the supplied approved copy and factual records. Permission restrictions in the owner's notes take precedence over inclusion in a source table.\n\nUse the attached brand identity and the source files listed in the asset manifest. The output register defines exact filenames, pages, sizes and record bindings. Supporting previews are welcome but cannot replace those files.",
  "brand_identity": {
    "brand_name": "Wharfside Folk Festival",
    "tagline": "Twenty years on the harbour",
    "sector": "Independent three night folk music festival producing a screen printed poster programme and act cards for its twentieth year.",
    "founded_place_size": "Founded 2006, on the working harbour at Fairhaven, Maine, a three night festival printed by a two person hand screen shop two streets away.",
    "about": "Wharfside is a three night folk festival on the working harbour at Fairhaven, in its twentieth year. Everything it prints comes off a two person hand screen shop that has printed the festival since the beginning, on a press that runs four inks plus the colour of the paper. The visible, hand pulled look is the festival's signature, and people frame the posters every year.",
    "personality": [
      "Handmade",
      "Rooted",
      "Folk",
      "Warm",
      "Community run",
      "Unpolished"
    ],
    "audience": "Festival goers and locals at thirty five to sixty dollar tickets, many of whom already own the last five years of posters and buy the new one as a twenty dollar framed keepsake.",
    "price_positioning": "Community festival pricing, tickets thirty five to sixty dollars and posters sold afterwards at twenty dollars. The slightly imperfect hand pulled screen look is the value, not a corner cut.",
    "palette": [
      {
        "name": "Harbour Blue",
        "hex": "#2F5A6E"
